{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1128,1360p;1425,1510p;1560,1640p;1680,1735p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1128\t## 8. The manifest registry\n  1129\t\n  1130\t### 8.1 The module manifest\n  1131\t\n  1132\tA manifest is content: one map, materialized in `dao.jing`, named by its\n  1133\taddress. It replaces the `{sym fn}` dictionary entry.\n  1134\t\n  1135\t```clojure\n  1136\t{:yin.module/name        'my.lib\n  1137\t :yin.module/schema      1                   ; this container's shape\n  1138\t :yin.module/contracts   {:yin.ast/code          \"v2\"   ; per format\n  1139\t                          :yin.semantic/code     \"v2\"\n  1140\t                          :yin.debruijn.code     \"b1\"\n  1141\t                          :yin.debruijn.register \"r1\"}\n  1142\t :yin.module/tree        :segment/...        ; the one canonical tree\n  1143\t :yin.module/derivations {:yin.semantic/code     :segment/...  ; record\n  1144\t                          :yin.debruijn.code     :segment/...  ; record\n  1145\t                          :yin.debruijn.register :segment/...} ; record\n  1146\t :yin.module/index       {H :segment/... R :segment/...}       ; optional\n  1147\t :yin.module/exports     #{'foo 'bar}\n  1148\t :yin.module/requires    {'other.lib :segment/...}             ; manifest\n  1149\t :yin.module/primitives  {'println :yin.k.pp/sha256-...}       ; profile\n  1150\t :yin.module/footprint   {:store-keys #{} :effects #{}}}       ; UCF 7.6.1\n  1151\t```\n  1152\t\n  1153\tRules:\n  1154\t\n  1155\t- **One tree.** `:yin.module/tree` is the root row id of the canonical\n  1156\t  AST the module was authored as. The `:yin.ast/code` image *is* this\n  1157\t  tree, so it has no derivation record.\n  1158\t- **One derivation record per lowered format.** Each value under\n  1159\t  `:yin.module/derivations` is the address of a content-addressed\n  1160\t  derivation record in the shape `yin.vm.ledger/derive-record` mints:\n  1161\t  `{:yin.ledger/op :derive :yin.ledger/input tree\n  1162\t  :yin.ledger/output identity :yin.ledger/function f\n  1163\t  :yin.ledger/profile {...}}`. The linker fetches the record (through a\n  1164\t  `:yin.ledger/record` format record: `segment-matches?` identity, a\n  1165\t  validator over these keys, no parts, no obligations) and checks\n  1166\t  `:yin.ledger/input` equals `:yin.module/tree` and `:yin.ledger/output`\n  1167\t  is the identity it then fetches. A record leading from a different\n  1168\t  tree, or to a different identity, is `:derivation-mismatch`. Four\n  1169\t  individually valid images from four different trees therefore cannot\n  1170\t  share a manifest, and a swapped image fails before load.\n  1171\t- **Three contracts, kept apart.** A manifest carries a schema version\n  1172\t  and a per-format contract map, and neither is the other:\n  1173\t  - `:yin.module/schema` versions the manifest container itself: which\n  1174\t    keys exist and what they mean. It is checked by the\n  1175\t    `:yin.module/manifest` format record's validator, which implements\n  1176\t    exactly one schema version; a manifest of another version is\n  1177\t    `:descriptor-defect` with rule `:schema`. It says nothing about any\n  1178\t    bytecode.\n  1179\t  - `:yin.module/contracts` maps each format the manifest lowered to\n  1180\t    the execution contract that format's image targets: the UCF stamp\n  1181\t    `\"v2\"` for the semantic vector and the tree, the B1 lowering\n  1182\t    contract `\"b1\"` for the stack image, the R1 contract `\"r1\"` for the\n  1183\t    register image. A format present under `:yin.module/derivations`\n  1184\t    must be present here; one that is not is `:descriptor-defect` with\n  1185\t    rule `:contract-missing`.\n  1186\t  - A format record's `:contract` (section 4.1) is the one execution\n  1187\t    contract that record implements, and a request's\n  1188\t    `:yin.link/contract` is the one the requester runs.\n  1189\t  **Contract before content.** Immediately after the manifest passes\n  1190\t  steps 2 to 4, `(get :yin.module/contracts format)` for the requested\n  1191\t  format is checked against the format record's `:contract`\n  1192\t  (`:contract-mismatch`), before the name check and before any\n  1193\t  derivation or image is fetched (section 4.2, step 0). A four-way\n  1194\t  manifest linking through the stack kernel therefore compares `\"b1\"`\n  1195\t  with `\"b1\"`, and the same manifest linking through the semantic\n  1196\t  kernel compares `\"v2\"` with `\"v2\"`; the tree's `\"v2\"` and the register\n  1197\t  image's `\"r1\"` play no part in either check. Revision r3 carried one\n  1198\t  `:yin.module/contract \"v2\"` and would have refused every stack and\n  1199\t  register link of a valid manifest; that was a defect.\n  1200\t- **Verifying and trusting are two policies, and verifying never\n  1201\t  trusts.** The linker's `:derivation` policy is one of `:verifying` or\n  1202\t  `:trusted`, chosen by the composition; there is no policy under which\n  1203\t  a verifying link accepts a claim it did not recompute.\n  1204\t  - Under `:verifying`, for every image it delivers the linker fetches\n  1205\t    the manifest's tree through the `:yin.ast/code` record (steps 2 to\n  1206\t    4, so the tree itself is verified), re-lowers it under the exact\n  1207\t    per-format profile the derivation record names (`\"ast-to-bytecode\"`\n  1208\t    for `:yin.semantic/code`, the B2 stack lowering for\n  1209\t    `:yin.debruijn.code`, the R1 register lowering for\n  1210\t    `:yin.debruijn.register`, each pinned by its own\n  1211\t    `:yin.ledger/profile` map), and compares the recomputed identity to\n  1212\t    `:yin.ledger/output` (`yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` section 5.2.2, step\n  1213\t    2). Inequality is `:derivation-mismatch`. If the linker does not\n  1214\t    implement that exact profile, or the tree is `:absent`, or the tree\n  1215\t    fails its own verification, the link is refused\n  1216\t    `:unverified-derivation` naming the profile and what was missing.\n  1217\t    It is never downgraded to trust.\n  1218\t  - Under `:trusted`, the linker checks only the record's input and\n  1219\t    output addresses (the rule above) and reports `:trust :composition`\n  1220\t    in the outcome, exactly as B6's trusted fallback did and never\n  1221\t    silently. A composition that chooses `:trusted` has chosen to\n  1222\t    accept the publisher's lowering, and the outcome says so.\n  1223\t  The B6 fallback pair maps onto these: `verifying-fallback` is the\n  1224\t  `:verifying` policy applied to an H image selected in place of an\n  1225\t  unsupported R; `trusted-fallback` is `:trusted` applied the same way.\n  1226\t  The `:yin.ast/code` image needs no derivation under either policy: it\n  1227\t  is the tree, verified by content.\n  1228\t- **The name is verified.** Immediately after the manifest passes steps\n  1229\t  2 to 4, the linker compares `:yin.module/name` with the\n  1230\t  `:yin.link/name` it was resolved under; inequality is\n  1231\t  `:module-name-mismatch` naming both. A name-environment entry can\n  1232\t  therefore point only at a manifest that claims that name.\n  1233\t- `:yin.module/index` maps contract-pinned identities to their storage\n  1234\t  addresses, the H and R indexes of B6 section 6 carried beside the\n  1235\t  identities they resolve. It is merged into linker-local `:indexes`\n  1236\t  when the manifest is verified, never consulted from the wire.\n  1237\t- `:yin.module/exports` are names, checked after the child evaluation\n  1238\t  (section 7.3). `:yin.module/requires` maps each required module to the\n  1239\t  manifest address the publisher linked against; `:yin.module/primitives`\n  1240\t  maps each assumed host function to its profile address (UCF section\n  1241\t  7.5.2). Together they are the declarations step 5a joins free names\n  1242\t  with.\n  1243\t- `:yin.module/footprint` is what `yin.vm.dependency-completion.md`\n  1244\t  needs to report `:complete`; an undeclared footprint is `:incomplete`,\n  1245\t  never a silent under-approximation.\n  1246\t- The manifest is verified like any content: a `:yin.module/manifest`\n  1247\t  format record with `:identity-matches-fn jing/segment-matches?`, a\n  1248\t  validator over the keys above, no parts, no obligations.\n  1249\t\n  1250\t### 8.2 The name environment and its authority\n  1251\t\n  1252\tNames live outside the manifest. A name environment maps a module name\n  1253\tto a manifest address and is linker-local state in one of two shapes:\n  1254\t\n  1255\t- a plain map `{'my.lib :segment/...}`, for tests and single-process\n  1256\t  compositions, with the composition itself as the sole asserter;\n  1257\t- assertions read from a `dao.space` source under the policy below.\n  1258\t\n  1259\t**Fail-closed assertion policy.** This policy is an entry criterion for\n  1260\tM4: no linker may resolve a name from `dao.space` assertions before it is\n  1261\timplemented and tested.\n  1262\t\n  1263\t- **Every authority event is a signed envelope.** An assertion and a\n  1264\t  retraction are two distinct envelope shapes, each a plain map whose\n  1265\t  content address (`dao.jing/segment-key`) is the event's id:\n  1266\t\n  1267\t  ```clojure\n  1268\t  ;; assertion\n  1269\t  {:yin.module/op          :assert\n  1270\t   :yin.module/name        'my.lib\n  1271\t   :yin.module/manifest    :segment/...\n  1272\t   :yin.module/asserted-by principal\n  1273\t   :yin.module/seq         41}          ; per-principal, strictly rising\n  1274\t\n  1275\t  ;; retraction: bound to one assertion by that assertion's id\n  1276\t  {:yin.module/op          :retract\n  1277\t   :yin.module/of          :segment/... ; segment-key of the assertion\n  1278\t   :yin.module/asserted-by principal\n  1279\t   :yin.module/seq         42}\n  1280\t  ```\n  1281\t\n  1282\t  The envelope is transacted as datoms `[ev :yin.module/envelope env]`\n  1283\t  and `[ev :yin.module/proof proof]`. An envelope is honored only with\n  1284\t  a proof; a bare `:asserted-by` value is a string anyone can write.\n  1285\t  An envelope whose proof is absent or fails is `:unauthenticated`\n  1286\t  with `:kind :no-proof` or `:bad-proof` and is discarded before\n  1287\t  counting. A retraction whose `:yin.module/of` names no assertion at\n  1288\t  the snapshot, or an assertion by a different principal, is discarded\n  1289\t  with `:kind :dangling-retraction`; a retraction retracts exactly the\n  1290\t  assertion it names and nothing by name alone.\n  1291\t- **Replay is prevented by the per-principal sequence.** Every envelope\n  1292\t  a principal issues carries `:yin.module/seq`, strictly increasing\n  1293\t  over that principal's lifetime; the composition declares each\n  1294\t  principal's floor in `:authority` (`0` for a new principal, the\n  1295\t  highest sequence already honored for a re-declared one). At the\n  1296\t  snapshot the linker orders one principal's proven envelopes by\n  1297\t  sequence and honors each only if its sequence exceeds every sequence\n  1298\t  honored before it; an envelope at or below the floor, or at or below\n  1299\t  an already honored sequence, is a replay and is discarded with\n  1300\t  `:kind :replay`. Two proven envelopes from one principal with equal\n  1301\t  sequence are equivocation: both are discarded, and the principal's\n  1302\t  later envelopes at the snapshot are discarded too. A monotone\n  1303\t  sequence is chosen over nonces because it makes the check stateless\n  1304\t  over the snapshot: no nonce store is needed and no window is guessed.\n  1305\t  A wall-clock timestamp is admitted as an optional\n  1306\t  `:yin.module/issued-at` in the envelope for audit, and is never used\n  1307\t  to order or to accept.\n  1308\t- Two proof kinds are admitted, and the composition's `:authority`\n  1309\t  declares, per principal, which one it expects:\n  1310\t  - *Signature.* `proof` is `{:yin.module/signature sig}`, where `sig`\n  1311\t    signs the canonical bytes (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`) of the whole\n  1312\t    envelope under the principal's public key, so operation type, name,\n  1313\t    manifest, principal, and sequence are all covered and none can be\n  1314\t    altered or recombined. `:authority` holds, per principal, the key\n  1315\t    and a composition-supplied verify function; the linker calls the\n  1316\t    function and implements no cryptographic primitive itself (a host\n  1317\t    library sits behind the function, as `dao.jing` does for hashing).\n  1318\t    The signature is over content, so it survives every carrier and\n  1319\t    can be checked by any host that holds the key.\n  1320\t  - *Attested log.* The assertion stream is a one-writer log\n  1321\t    (`dao.stream.md`, *Concurrency*) whose writer the composition\n  1322\t    authenticated at attachment and bound to one principal; `:authority`\n  1323\t    names the stream's `:dao.stream/identity` beside that principal, and\n  1324\t    every envelope read from that identity, at the snapshot, counts as\n  1325\t    proven by it; `proof` is `{:yin.module/attested identity}` and the\n  1326\t    linker checks that the envelope was in fact read from that stream.\n  1327\t    The sequence rule applies unchanged, so a log that repeats an\n  1328\t    envelope repeats a replay. The proof holds only within the reach of\n  1329\t    the attachment discipline: an envelope copied off that log onto\n  1330\t    another medium carries no proof and is `:unauthenticated` there. A\n  1331\t    composition that needs envelopes to travel uses signatures.\n  1332\t  A principal declared with neither kind cannot assert anything.\n  1333\t- The linker's `:authority` names the accepted principals with their\n  1334\t  proof kind and material, and the **snapshot**: either a published\n  1335\t  index manifest address (`dao.space.index`) or a cursor position on\n  1336\t  the assertion stream. The linker reads exactly that snapshot;\n  1337\t  assertions appended afterwards do not exist for it until the\n  1338\t  composition advances the snapshot, which is an ordinary `link-state`\n  1339\t  rebuild, never an ambient re-read.\n  1340\t- At the snapshot, for one name: unauthenticated envelopes, replays,\n  1341\t  equivocations, and envelopes by undeclared principals are discarded;\n  1342\t  each honored retraction removes exactly the assertion its\n  1343\t  `:yin.module/of` names; the distinct manifest addresses remaining are\n  1344\t  counted. Exactly one resolves the name. Zero is `:absent`. More than\n  1345\t  one is `:ambiguous-name` naming every remaining address and asserter,\n  1346\t  and no address is chosen by recency, sequence, order, or any other\n  1347\t  rule.\n  1348\t- Provenance is data the outcome carries: a successful resolution names\n  1349\t  the asserter, the proof kind, and the snapshot under\n  1350\t  `:yin.link/provenance` so a receiver can record which claim it acted\n  1351\t  on.\n  1352\t\n  1353\tAn entry is a claim. The manifest it names is verified, and its name is\n  1354\tverified against the entry (section 8.1). Which principals a composition\n  1355\tdeclares, and how it obtains and rotates their keys, is the composition's\n  1356\t(section 12); what the linker does with a declared principal's assertion\n  1357\tis fixed above.\n  1358\t\n  1359\t### 8.3 What `yin.vm.module` becomes\n  1360\t\n  1425\tdeployed registries, and a clean break is the default here.\n  1426\t\n  1427\t## 9. Migration from `yin.vm.debruijn-linker`\n  1428\t\n  1429\tFive steps, each landing green on all three hosts before the next. The\n  1430\tpredecessor namespace is renamed, not aliased.\n  1431\t\n  1432\t```mermaid\n  1433\tflowchart TD\n  1434\t  M1[\"M1 rename\\nyin.vm.debruijn-linker -> yin.vm.linker\"]\n  1435\t  M2[\"M2 four format records\\nidentity-directed match, bounded parts\"]\n  1436\t  M3[\"M3 stepped core + link runtime\\nfetch = host policy; DHT behind server\"]\n  1437\t  M4[\"M4 require lowers to the linker\\nmanifests, authority, child install\"]\n  1438\t  M5[\"M5 yin.repl wires the four streams\\nper backend\"]\n  1439\t  M1 --> M2 --> M3 --> M4 --> M5\n  1440\t```\n  1441\t\n  1442\t**M1. Rename.** Move `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc` to\n  1443\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc` with namespace `yin.vm.linker`; move the\n  1444\ttest likewise. Update the five design documents that name the old\n  1445\tnamespace (`yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md`, `yin.vm.debruijn.register.md`,\n  1446\t`dao.agent.md`, `dao.agent.harness.md`, `dao.agent.mcp.server.md`) and\n  1447\tthe orchestrator log. Mark `yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md` as superseded by\n  1448\tthis document in its status line. No behavior changes. The B6 test\n  1449\tsuite passes unchanged apart from the require alias.\n  1450\t\n  1451\t**M2. Four format records.** Replace `:hash-fn` with `:identity-fn` and\n  1452\t`:identity-matches-fn`; rename `:free-names-fn` to `:obligations-fn`;\n  1453\tadd `:contract`, `:row-defect-fn`, and `:parts-fn`; add `ast-format`,\n  1454\t`semantic-format`, `semantic-free-names`, and `row-local-defect`. Make\n  1455\tstep 2 the bounded worklist. `yin.vm.content` keeps `materialize-tree!`\n  1456\tand `materialize-vector!` as the mint side (they are `publish!` for those\n  1457\tformats); `load-rows` and `fetch-vector` are retired, and their callers\n  1458\tmove to `fetch` with the new records. Tests, beyond B6's matrix for the\n  1459\ttwo new formats: a tree with one absent child row is `:absent` naming\n  1460\tthat row; a tree with one corrupt child row is `:address-mismatch`\n  1461\tnaming it; a tree whose root is well-formed but whose child has a bad\n  1462\ttag is `:descriptor-defect` with no fetch of that child's slots; a tree\n  1463\texceeding `:max-parts` is `:parts-limit`; a vector whose index entry\n  1464\tpoints at a different valid vector is `:hash-mismatch`; a vector minted\n  1465\tunder `:sha256` verifies against its own address while the default is\n  1466\t`:blake3`.\n  1467\t\n  1468\t**M3. Stepped core and link runtime.** Implement `link-state`,\n  1469\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon` over `dao.jing.remote.step` (or, for a\n  1470\tpurely local composition, over `dao.stream.rpc` on a ring-buffer pair\n  1471\tserved by `dao.jing.remote/serve-content!`'s handlers). Reimplement\n  1472\t`fetch` as the blocking driver over a link runtime; export `verify` and\n  1473\t`discharge`. Tests: the full refusal matrix through `step` over ring\n  1474\tbuffers on all three hosts; the JVM WebSocket path from B6 completion\n  1475\tcriterion 1; a `:pending` sequence where the content server answers one\n  1476\tpart per step; a request carrying a function or a handle is\n  1477\t`:invalid-request`; the local-fetch traffic test of section 6.4 with a\n  1478\t`get`-counting server handle and a handle-free linker state; the DHT\n  1479\thandle behind `serve-content!` answering a link over ring buffers with\n  1480\tthe server driven by the test.\n  1481\t\n  1482\t**M4. `require` lowers to the linker.** Entry criterion: the section 8.2\n  1483\tassertion policy is implemented and its tests pass (a signed assertion\n  1484\tby a declared principal resolves; a bare `:asserted-by` with no proof is\n  1485\t`:unauthenticated`; a bad signature is `:unauthenticated`; an attested\n  1486\tlog's assertion copied onto another stream is `:unauthenticated`; an\n  1487\tundeclared principal is ignored; a signed retraction bound to an\n  1488\tassertion's id removes that assertion only, and a retraction naming no\n  1489\tassertion or signed by another principal is discarded; a replayed\n  1490\tsequence and an equivocating pair are discarded; two proven assertions\n  1491\trefuse `:ambiguous-name`; snapshot advance). Then: the manifest and\n  1492\tderivation\n  1493\tformat records; `register-host-module` with profile enforcement;\n  1494\t`require-handler` minting, parking, and emitting; the two wait states\n  1495\tthrough `check-wait-set` with id correlation; the install child in the\n  1496\tscheduler with the section 7.3 phases; `link-module`; the UCF table\n  1497\tamendments. Tests, per backend: a require of an unlinked module over\n  1498\tring buffers completes and the program resumes with its exports bound;\n  1499\ta manifest declaring a different name is `:module-name-mismatch`; a\n  1500\tmanifest whose semantic, H, or R derivation leads from a different tree\n  1501\tis `:derivation-mismatch` (three swapped-image tests, and a fourth\n  1502\twhere the `:yin.ast/code` tree is not the manifest's tree); a\n  1503\tsame-named primitive of different profile at the receiver is\n  1504\t`:unresolved-free`; a shadowed export name in the requiring program's\n  1505\tstore is `:shadowed-free`; a free name the manifest never declares is\n  1506\t`:undeclared-free`; two outstanding requires on one response stream\n  1507\teach restore on their own id; a response landing before the entry would\n  1508\thave been polled is not skipped; a module requiring another links\n  1509\ttransitively while a third task keeps running; a require cycle is\n  1510\t`:require-cycle`; `(vm :stack)` and `(vm :register)` in `yin.repl` link\n  1560\t## 11. Completion criteria\n  1561\t\n  1562\tStructure:\n  1563\t\n  1564\t1. One `fetch` and one `step` serve all four formats with no\n  1565\t   format-specific branching; a fifth format is one record.\n  1566\t2. No global loader, registry, callback, or cache; every input is an\n  1567\t   argument or VM-state value; no function or handle ever appears in a\n  1568\t   value on the link or content streams.\n  1569\t3. Tri-host parity (JVM, Node, ClojureDart), 0 kondo errors, clean\n  1570\t   cljstyle.\n  1571\t4. This file and `yin.vm.linker` are pure ASCII with every line at most\n  1572\t   80 columns.\n  1573\t\n  1574\tVerification:\n  1575\t\n  1576\t5. Every B6 completion criterion (section 11 there) holds for all four\n  1577\t   formats where applicable, through both `fetch` and `step`.\n  1578\t6. A payload whose address is valid but whose identity is not the one\n  1579\t   requested is refused for every format, including the two whose\n  1580\t   identity is a storage address, and under every registered algorithm.\n  1581\t7. A request naming a contract the format record does not implement is\n  1582\t   `:contract-mismatch` before validation runs.\n  1583\t8. A malformed row is refused before any of its children is requested,\n  1584\t   and every composition bound produces `:parts-limit`.\n  1585\t9. Local `fetch` produces exactly the content-pair traffic the stepped\n  1586\t   path produces and holds no content handle.\n  1587\t\n  1588\tRequire:\n  1589\t\n  1590\t10. `(require 'foo)` on each of the four backends, over ring buffers,\n  1591\t    parks, links, installs through the child phases, and resumes with\n  1592\t    `'foo`; the same over the JVM WebSocket content path.\n  1593\t11. The registry value holds no function that arrived by linking; every\n  1594\t    linked module's `:bindings` came from an isolated child evaluation\n  1595\t    that reached halt with every export bound.\n  1596\t12. UCF section 7.4.1 carries `:link-request`, `:link-response`, and\n  1597\t    `:install` safepoints, section 7.4.3 their pending variants, section\n  1598\t    7.5.1 the `:yin.k/binding` closure variants of section 7.3, and a\n  1599\t    parked entry of each kind lifts and lowers through UCF's round-trip\n  1600\t    test.\n  1601\t13. Every swapped-image and swapped-name case in M4 refuses before load.\n  1602\t14. The assertion policy of section 8.2 refuses `:ambiguous-name`,\n  1603\t    discards unproven assertions as `:unauthenticated`, and ignores\n  1604\t    undeclared principals, at a fixed snapshot.\n  1605\t15. A module that defines a name and then reads it produces no\n  1606\t    obligation for that name; a main-sequence read before the\n  1607\t    definition is `:use-before-definition`; a read inside a body\n  1608\t    defined later in the main sequence produces no obligation; an\n  1609\t    export whose key is computed at run time is neither refused\n  1610\t    statically nor assumed, and is verified at `validated`.\n  1611\t16. Two install children and the root task, each with counter `0`,\n  1612\t    issue three requests on one link pair with three distinct ids, and\n  1613\t    each restores on its own.\n  1614\t17. On every backend, an exported closure applied in the parent after\n  1615\t    `linked` runs the same body it ran in the child; a stack and a\n  1616\t    register closure exported from a child whose image was appended at\n  1617\t    a nonzero offset in the parent resolve to the relocated pc.\n  1618\t18. Under `:derivation :verifying`, a manifest whose record names a\n  1619\t    profile the linker does not implement is `:unverified-derivation`,\n  1620\t    never installed; under `:trusted` the same manifest installs with\n  1621\t    `:trust :composition` in the outcome.\n  1622\t19. A request naming a mismatched contract is refused with no content\n  1623\t    request appended and no validator run.\n  1624\t20. A closure re-exported from a transitive dependency lifts with that\n  1625\t    dependency's image as origin, the parent loads that image before\n  1626\t    lowering, and an origin the scheduler never verified is\n  1627\t    `:foreign-image`; a positional marker offered to a named kernel is\n  1628\t    `:binding-mismatch`.\n  1629\t21. A replayed envelope, an envelope at or below a principal's floor,\n  1630\t    two envelopes with one sequence, a retraction naming no assertion,\n  1631\t    and a retraction by another principal are each discarded with the\n  1632\t    stated kind; a retraction bound to an assertion's id removes that\n  1633\t    assertion only.\n  1634\t22. One four-way manifest links through all four kernels with no\n  1635\t    `:contract-mismatch`; a manifest of another schema version is\n  1636\t    `:descriptor-defect` with rule `:schema`; a derivation without a\n  1637\t    contract entry is `:descriptor-defect` with rule\n  1638\t    `:contract-missing`.\n  1639\t\n  1640\t## 12. Open decisions\n  1680\t\n  1681\t## 13. Reconciliation record\n  1682\t\n  1683\t### 13.1 Revision r4 (round 3, `gpt-6-sol`)\n  1684\t\n  1685\tThe round-3 review closed round-2 items 1, 3, 5, 7, and 10 and left four\n  1686\tpartial plus one example defect. Each, and what r4 did:\n  1687\t\n  1688\t| Item                              | Resolution                        |\n  1689\t|-----------------------------------|-----------------------------------|\n  1690\t| Naive subtract-all of definitions | Agreed. Defined-before-use:       |\n  1691\t| and static export refusal         | main-sequence occurrences need a  |\n  1692\t|                                   | preceding definition or are       |\n  1693\t|                                   | `:use-before-definition`; body    |\n  1694\t|                                   | occurrences accept any definition;|\n  1695\t|                                   | static export refusal withdrawn,  |\n  1696\t|                                   | exports verified only at          |\n  1697\t|                                   | `validated` (4.1, 4.2 step 5a).   |\n  1698\t| Two scalar id examples left       | Agreed. Completion examples now   |\n  1699\t|                                   | carry `[:t0 7]` (6.3).            |\n  1700\t| Closure origin, transitive images,| Agreed. Lift records the origin   |\n  1701\t| and the named/positional mapping  | image from the offset table or    |\n  1702\t|                                   | alias column; origin set checked  |\n  1703\t|                                   | against verified images           |\n  1704\t|                                   | (`:foreign-image`); parent loads  |\n  1705\t|                                   | every origin before lowering;     |\n  1706\t|                                   | `:yin.k/binding :named` and       |\n  1707\t|                                   | `:positional` variants with lift  |\n  1708\t|                                   | and lower tables;                 |\n  1709\t|                                   | `:binding-mismatch` (7.3).        |\n  1710\t| Assertion signatures, retraction  | Agreed. Distinct signed envelopes |\n  1711\t| binding, and replay               | for assert and retract covering   |\n  1712\t|                                   | op, name, manifest, principal,    |\n  1713\t|                                   | sequence; retraction bound by the |\n  1714\t|                                   | assertion's content id;           |\n  1715\t|                                   | per-principal monotone sequence   |\n  1716\t|                                   | with floors, replay and           |\n  1717\t|                                   | equivocation discarded (8.2).     |\n  1718\t|                                   | Divergence: a sequence rather     |\n  1719\t|                                   | than nonces, so the snapshot      |\n  1720\t|                                   | check is stateless; timestamps    |\n  1721\t|                                   | are audit-only.                   |\n  1722\t| One manifest contract failed      | Agreed; r3 defect. `:yin.module/  |\n  1723\t| stack and register links          | schema` versions the container;   |\n  1724\t|                                   | `:yin.module/contracts` maps each |\n  1725\t|                                   | format to its execution contract; |\n  1726\t|                                   | step 0 compares the requested     |\n  1727\t|                                   | format's entry only (8.1, 4.2).   |\n  1728\t\n  1729\t### 13.2 Revision r3 (round 2, `gpt-6-sol`)\n  1730\t\n  1731\tThe round-2 review verified round-1 items 1, 7, 9a to 9e, and 10 as\n  1732\tclosed and marked seven items partial plus one ordering defect. Each,\n  1733\tand what r3 did:\n  1734\t\n  1735\t| Item                              | Resolution                        |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
