{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1250,1357p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1250\t### 8.2 The name environment and its authority\n  1251\t\n  1252\tNames live outside the manifest. A name environment maps a module name\n  1253\tto a manifest address and is linker-local state in one of two shapes:\n  1254\t\n  1255\t- a plain map `{'my.lib :segment/...}`, for tests and single-process\n  1256\t  compositions, with the composition itself as the sole asserter;\n  1257\t- assertions read from a `dao.space` source under the policy below.\n  1258\t\n  1259\t**Fail-closed assertion policy.** This policy is an entry criterion for\n  1260\tM4: no linker may resolve a name from `dao.space` assertions before it is\n  1261\timplemented and tested.\n  1262\t\n  1263\t- **Every authority event is a signed envelope.** An assertion and a\n  1264\t  retraction are two distinct envelope shapes, each a plain map whose\n  1265\t  content address (`dao.jing/segment-key`) is the event's id:\n  1266\t\n  1267\t  ```clojure\n  1268\t  ;; assertion\n  1269\t  {:yin.module/op          :assert\n  1270\t   :yin.module/name        'my.lib\n  1271\t   :yin.module/manifest    :segment/...\n  1272\t   :yin.module/asserted-by principal\n  1273\t   :yin.module/seq         41}          ; per-principal, strictly rising\n  1274\t\n  1275\t  ;; retraction: bound to one assertion by that assertion's id\n  1276\t  {:yin.module/op          :retract\n  1277\t   :yin.module/of          :segment/... ; segment-key of the assertion\n  1278\t   :yin.module/asserted-by principal\n  1279\t   :yin.module/seq         42}\n  1280\t  ```\n  1281\t\n  1282\t  The envelope is transacted as datoms `[ev :yin.module/envelope env]`\n  1283\t  and `[ev :yin.module/proof proof]`. An envelope is honored only with\n  1284\t  a proof; a bare `:asserted-by` value is a string anyone can write.\n  1285\t  An envelope whose proof is absent or fails is `:unauthenticated`\n  1286\t  with `:kind :no-proof` or `:bad-proof` and is discarded before\n  1287\t  counting. A retraction whose `:yin.module/of` names no assertion at\n  1288\t  the snapshot, or an assertion by a different principal, is discarded\n  1289\t  with `:kind :dangling-retraction`; a retraction retracts exactly the\n  1290\t  assertion it names and nothing by name alone.\n  1291\t- **Replay is prevented by the per-principal sequence.** Every envelope\n  1292\t  a principal issues carries `:yin.module/seq`, strictly increasing\n  1293\t  over that principal's lifetime; the composition declares each\n  1294\t  principal's floor in `:authority` (`0` for a new principal, the\n  1295\t  highest sequence already honored for a re-declared one). At the\n  1296\t  snapshot the linker orders one principal's proven envelopes by\n  1297\t  sequence and honors each only if its sequence exceeds every sequence\n  1298\t  honored before it; an envelope at or below the floor, or at or below\n  1299\t  an already honored sequence, is a replay and is discarded with\n  1300\t  `:kind :replay`. Two proven envelopes from one principal with equal\n  1301\t  sequence are equivocation: both are discarded, and the principal's\n  1302\t  later envelopes at the snapshot are discarded too. A monotone\n  1303\t  sequence is chosen over nonces because it makes the check stateless\n  1304\t  over the snapshot: no nonce store is needed and no window is guessed.\n  1305\t  A wall-clock timestamp is admitted as an optional\n  1306\t  `:yin.module/issued-at` in the envelope for audit, and is never used\n  1307\t  to order or to accept.\n  1308\t- Two proof kinds are admitted, and the composition's `:authority`\n  1309\t  declares, per principal, which one it expects:\n  1310\t  - *Signature.* `proof` is `{:yin.module/signature sig}`, where `sig`\n  1311\t    signs the canonical bytes (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`) of the whole\n  1312\t    envelope under the principal's public key, so operation type, name,\n  1313\t    manifest, principal, and sequence are all covered and none can be\n  1314\t    altered or recombined. `:authority` holds, per principal, the key\n  1315\t    and a composition-supplied verify function; the linker calls the\n  1316\t    function and implements no cryptographic primitive itself (a host\n  1317\t    library sits behind the function, as `dao.jing` does for hashing).\n  1318\t    The signature is over content, so it survives every carrier and\n  1319\t    can be checked by any host that holds the key.\n  1320\t  - *Attested log.* The assertion stream is a one-writer log\n  1321\t    (`dao.stream.md`, *Concurrency*) whose writer the composition\n  1322\t    authenticated at attachment and bound to one principal; `:authority`\n  1323\t    names the stream's `:dao.stream/identity` beside that principal, and\n  1324\t    every envelope read from that identity, at the snapshot, counts as\n  1325\t    proven by it; `proof` is `{:yin.module/attested identity}` and the\n  1326\t    linker checks that the envelope was in fact read from that stream.\n  1327\t    The sequence rule applies unchanged, so a log that repeats an\n  1328\t    envelope repeats a replay. The proof holds only within the reach of\n  1329\t    the attachment discipline: an envelope copied off that log onto\n  1330\t    another medium carries no proof and is `:unauthenticated` there. A\n  1331\t    composition that needs envelopes to travel uses signatures.\n  1332\t  A principal declared with neither kind cannot assert anything.\n  1333\t- The linker's `:authority` names the accepted principals with their\n  1334\t  proof kind and material, and the **snapshot**: either a published\n  1335\t  index manifest address (`dao.space.index`) or a cursor position on\n  1336\t  the assertion stream. The linker reads exactly that snapshot;\n  1337\t  assertions appended afterwards do not exist for it until the\n  1338\t  composition advances the snapshot, which is an ordinary `link-state`\n  1339\t  rebuild, never an ambient re-read.\n  1340\t- At the snapshot, for one name: unauthenticated envelopes, replays,\n  1341\t  equivocations, and envelopes by undeclared principals are discarded;\n  1342\t  each honored retraction removes exactly the assertion its\n  1343\t  `:yin.module/of` names; the distinct manifest addresses remaining are\n  1344\t  counted. Exactly one resolves the name. Zero is `:absent`. More than\n  1345\t  one is `:ambiguous-name` naming every remaining address and asserter,\n  1346\t  and no address is chosen by recency, sequence, order, or any other\n  1347\t  rule.\n  1348\t- Provenance is data the outcome carries: a successful resolution names\n  1349\t  the asserter, the proof kind, and the snapshot under\n  1350\t  `:yin.link/provenance` so a receiver can record which claim it acted\n  1351\t  on.\n  1352\t\n  1353\tAn entry is a claim. The manifest it names is verified, and its name is\n  1354\tverified against the entry (section 8.1). Which principals a composition\n  1355\tdeclares, and how it obtains and rotates their keys, is the composition's\n  1356\t(section 12); what the linker does with a declared principal's assertion\n  1357\tis fixed above.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '705,762p;875,910p;1530,1558p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '705,762p;875,910p;1530,1558p'\"","aggregated_output":"   705\talready has, the portable linker is a pure function over explicit state.\n   706\t\n   707\t```clojure\n   708\t(link-state opts)               ; -> state; no socket, atom, or scheduler\n   709\t(request-link state request)    ; -> [state link-id]\n   710\t(step state budget)             ; -> {:state s :completions [...]\n   711\t                                ;     :diagnostics [...]}\n   712\t(abandon state link-id reason)  ; -> state\n   713\t```\n   714\t\n   715\tA `request` is plain data and nothing else. Its closed key set is\n   716\t`:yin.link/id`, `:yin.link/format`, `:yin.link/contract` (optional), and\n   717\texactly one of `:yin.link/name` or `:yin.link/identity`. The two\n   718\tadmissible shapes:\n   719\t\n   720\t```clojure\n   721\t;; by module name: the linker resolves the manifest (section 8)\n   722\t{:yin.link/id       [:t0 7]                  ; section 7.2, step 3\n   723\t :yin.link/format   :yin.debruijn.code\n   724\t :yin.link/contract \"b1\"\n   725\t :yin.link/name     'my.lib}\n   726\t\n   727\t;; by bare identity: B6's closed-image path, no manifest\n   728\t{:yin.link/id       [:t0 8]\n   729\t :yin.link/format   :yin.debruijn.code\n   730\t :yin.link/contract \"b1\"\n   731\t :yin.link/identity H}\n   732\t```\n   733\t\n   734\tA request carrying both `:yin.link/name` and `:yin.link/identity`, or\n   735\tneither, is `:invalid-request`, as is any key outside the set or any\n   736\tvalue that is not a scalar, keyword, symbol, address, or the id vector.\n   737\tA request carries no index, no receiver, no function, and no handle. The\n   738\trefusal is appended on the response stream under the request's id where\n   739\tthe id is well formed, and under `:yin.link/id nil` otherwise; it is\n   740\tnever processed further. The receiver's capabilities do not travel\n   741\tbecause discharge happens at the receiver (section 4.2, 5b).\n   742\t\n   743\t`step` advances every in-flight link in a fixed order: re-attempt\n   744\tunsent content requests, poll the content response medium at most\n   745\t`budget` elements, route each correlated response to its link, run the\n   746\tverification step that response enables, issue the next content request\n   747\tthe worklist needs (a part, under `:parts-fn`), and take completions.\n   748\tEach link is a small state machine over the six steps; steps 3 to 5a\n   749\tnever touch a stream and run the moment step 2 completes.\n   750\t\n   751\tA completion is the step-6 result or a refusal, tagged with its link id:\n   752\t\n   753\t```clojure\n   754\t{:yin.link/id [:t0 7] :status :ok :manifest m :derivation d\n   755\t :image {...} :obligations [...]}\n   756\t{:yin.link/id [:t0 7] :status :refused :reason :absent :address a}\n   757\t```\n   758\t\n   759\tA link with no completion yet is `:pending`; the caller steps again\n   760\twhen it chooses. Retry cadence, deadlines, and permanent-absence policy\n   761\tare the composition's, as D6 states: streams report, they do not decide.\n   762\t\n   875\t   share one response stream: the root task and every install child\n   876\t   (section 7.3) each have their own engine and their own `:id-counter`,\n   877\t   so a counter alone collides. A link id is therefore the pair\n   878\t   `[origin counter]`: `origin` is a task origin tag the scheduler that\n   879\t   owns the link pair mints from its own counter when it creates a task\n   880\t   (the root task at start, each child at `loading`), unique among every\n   881\t   task that has ever written to that pair; `counter` is the task's own\n   882\t   engine gensym. The scheduler never reuses an origin tag and a task\n   883\t   never reuses a counter, so no two requests on one pair share an id.\n   884\t   A composition that multiplexes several schedulers onto one pair must\n   885\t   give each scheduler a distinct origin prefix as composition data;\n   886\t   two schedulers on one pair with one prefix is a host assembly defect.\n   887\t4. **The request is appended; `ok` moves the entry to the response\n   888\t   state.** The handler appends `:envelope` through the link request\n   889\t   writer the composition supplied in `opts`. On `ok` the entry becomes\n   890\t   `{:reason :link-response :link-id 7 :response ... :cursor ...}`. On\n   891\t   `full` the entry stays in `:link-request` with its envelope retained\n   892\t   verbatim and is retried on the next poll, the `:ffi-request`\n   893\t   discipline. The two states are the two UCF pending variants this\n   894\t   flow adds (section 11, item 10): `:link-request` carries everything\n   895\t   needed to rebuild the envelope, `:link-response` carries the response\n   896\t   descriptor and the kept cell.\n   897\t5. **The linker interpreter observes the request stream** with its own\n   898\t   cursor, in its own control flow. It resolves the name through its\n   899\t   name environment at the snapshot it was composed with (section 8.2),\n   900\t   fetches the manifest by address through the `:yin.module/manifest`\n   901\t   format record so the manifest itself passes steps 2 to 4, checks the\n   902\t   manifest's declared name (section 8.1), selects the derivation and\n   903\t   identity for the requested format, verifies the derivation, and runs\n   904\t   the six steps for the image through the stepped core. A manifest with\n   905\t   no derivation for the requested format is `:unsupported-format`, and\n   906\t   the composed `:fallback` policy (section 5.5) applies, under the\n   907\t   composed `:derivation` policy, before a refusal is appended.\n   908\t6. **The response is appended** to the link response stream with the\n   909\t   request's exact `:yin.link/id`, as `:ok` with the image, manifest,\n   910\t   derivation, and obligations, or as the refusal. The linker holds\n  1530\t          test/yin/vm/linker_authority_test.cljc      (M4 entry)\n  1531\t          test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc        (M4)\n  1532\tEdited:   src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc                 (M4)\n  1533\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc  (:link-request, :link-response,\n  1534\t                                        :install wait reasons; the\n  1535\t                                        install child)             (M4)\n  1536\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/content.cljc (retire load-rows,\n  1537\t                                        fetch-vector)              (M2)\n  1538\t          src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc                      (M5)\n  1539\t          docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\n  1540\t            (section 7.4.1 rows, section 7.4.3 variants)           (M4)\n  1541\tDepends:  dao.jing (segment-key, segment-matches?, materialize!)\n  1542\t          dao.jing.remote, dao.jing.remote.step, dao.stream.rpc\n  1543\t          yin.vm (validate-rows, free-names, primitive-profiles)\n  1544\t          yin.vm.code (well-formed-vector?)\n  1545\t          yin.vm.ledger (derive-record, verify-derivation)\n  1546\t          yin.vm.debruijn-code, yin.vm.debruijn-register-code\n  1547\tMust not change:\n  1548\t          image-hash, register-hash, segment-key, the opcode\n  1549\t          tables, dao.stream, dao.jing, any kernel's step function\n  1550\t```\n  1551\t\n  1552\t`yin.vm.linker` exports: `fetch`, `verify`, `discharge`, `link-state`,\n  1553\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon`, `publish!`, `ast-format`,\n  1554\t`semantic-format`, `stack-format`, `register-format`, `manifest-format`,\n  1555\t`record-format`, the four free-name scanners, the four definition\n  1556\tscanners, `row-local-defect`, `index-from-datoms`, `address-attribute`,\n  1557\t`trusted-fallback`, `verifying-fallback`, `refused`, `refused?`, `ok?`,\n  1558\t`refusal-reasons`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
