e (fn [inst [i [_ kind]]]\n    97\t            (if (= :pc kind) (update inst (inc i) + offset) inst))\n    98\t          inst\n    99\t          (map-indexed vector (get opcode-table (nth inst 0)))))\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\t(defn- append-stack-image\n   103\t  \"Load `image` after the stack image `vm` already holds and start at its\n   104\t   first instruction.  A closure a previous input stored (a `def`) names a\n   105\t   body pc in the earlier image, so that image is kept, not replaced.\n   106\t   `:hash` stays the canonical H of the whole loaded `:segment`\n   107\t   (yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md), so each load hashes the concatenation.\"\n   108\t  [vm image]\n   109\t  (let [held (:segment vm)\n   110\t        offset (count held)\n   111\t        shift #(relocate dcode/opcode-table offset %)]\n   112\t    (assoc (stack/load-image vm (into held (map shift) image))\n   113\t           :pc offset)))\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\t(defn- append-register-image\n   117\t  \"The register image counterpart of `append-stack-image`.  The incoming\n   118\t   image is validated alone by `load-image`, which also sizes the register\n   119\t   file for its main body; the image it runs in is the concatenation, whose\n   120\t   later main bodies end in `:halt` as the first does.  `:hash` is the\n   121\t   canonical R of that concatenation (yin.vm.debruijn.register.md).\"\n   122\t  [vm {:keys [bodies instructions] :as image}]\n   123\t  (let [held (:segment vm)\n   124\t        offset (count (:instructions held))\n   125\t        shift-body #(-> % (update :start + offset) (update :end + offset))\n   126\t        shift #(relocate rcode/opcode-table offset %)\n   127\t        combined {:bodies (into (:bodies held) (map shift-body) bodies)\n   128\t                  :instructions (into (:instructions held)\n   129\t                                      (map shift)\n   130\t                                      instructions)}]\n   131\t    (assoc (register/load-image vm image)\n   132\t           :segment combined\n   133\t           :hash (rcode/register-hash combined)\n   134\t           :pc offset)))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t(def program-loaders\n   138\t  \"The loader the evaluator observer hands each `program-out` value, per\n   139\t   evaluator.  Every value there is one expanded canonical tree packet\n    90\t(def format-tag\n    91\t  \"The model tag every register payload carries as `:format`.\"\n    92\t  :yin.debruijn.code)\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\t(defn load-image\n    96\t  \"Load `segment` (a vector of instructions) into `vm` as its one image:\n    97\t   H is recomputed, the registers are reset to pc 0 with empty frames,\n    98\t   stack, and continuation, and the machine is running unless the segment\n    99\t   is empty. The store, the parked map, the wait set, the ready queue,\n   100\t   the id counter, and the composition values survive, exactly as they\n   101\t   survive a `yin.vm.semantic/load-vector`. A continuation parked under an\n   102\t   earlier image cannot be restored against this one: `stack-restore`\n   103\t   refuses it by H.\"\n   104\t  [vm segment]\n   105\t  (assoc vm\n   106\t         :segment segment\n   107\t         :hash (dcode/image-hash segment)\n   108\t         :pc 0\n   109\t         :frames []\n   110\t         :stack []\n   111\t         :continuation []\n   112\t         :halted? (empty? segment)\n   113\t         :blocked? false\n   114\t         :value nil))\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t(defn create-vm\n   118\t  \"Build a fresh `DebruijnVM` over `segment` (a vector of instructions).\n   119\t\n   120\t   Options: `:free-env`, `:store`, `:primitives`, `:modules` (all default to\n   121\t   `{}`, matching the named VM's empty defaults except that `:primitives`\n   122\t   defaults to `{}` here whereas `yin.vm/empty-state` populates the full\n   123\t   primitive table; callers pass `yin.vm/primitives` when they want the\n   124\t   standard registry), `:make-stream` (the 