{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '528,567p;719,770p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc | sed -n '132,150p'; rg -n 'defn vm-load-rows|vm-load-rows' src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   528\t(defn load-image\n   529\t  \"Decode one `:yin.code/*` batch into an executable image.\n   530\t\n   531\t   Returns `{:segment id, :length n, :code instructions}` where `instructions`\n   532\t   is a vector indexed by pc of decoded `[opcode & operands]` vectors with\n   533\t   every `:yin.code/target` and `:yin.code/body` ref resolved to a pc integer\n   534\t   of the same segment, plus `:address` when the segment entity carries\n   535\t   `:yin.code/hash` (§2.2) — a claim checked here: the canonical vector the\n   536\t   batch reconstructs to must hash to it (UCF §7.3.4's content-integrity\n   537\t   check, its `:yin.k/hash-mismatch` outcome), so a false claim never\n   538\t   reaches the alias column. Throws a load error naming the entity and rule\n   539\t   when the batch is not well formed (§2.6); the loader is total over the\n   540\t   outcomes of its inputs and does not guess.\"\n   541\t  [datoms]\n   542\t  (let [defect (code/well-formed? datoms)]\n   543\t    (when defect\n   544\t      (throw (ex-info (str \"Cannot load segment: \" (name (:rule defect))\n   545\t                           \" (entity \" (:entity defect) \")\")\n   546\t                      {:defect defect})))\n   547\t    (let [[order attrs] (index-batch datoms)\n   548\t          segments (filterv #(= :segment (get-in attrs [% :yin.code/type]))\n   549\t                            order)\n   550\t          seg (first segments)\n   551\t          structural [:yin.code/segment :yin.code/pc :yin.code/op]\n   552\t          instructions (filterv (fn [e]\n   553\t                                  (and (not= seg e)\n   554\t                                       (some #(contains? (get attrs e) %)\n   555\t                                             structural)))\n   556\t                                order)\n   557\t          ;; Rule 3 sorts by pc, so an instruction's position is its pc.\n   558\t          pc-of (zipmap instructions (range))\n   559\t          resolve-ref (fn [e ref]\n   560\t                        (or (get pc-of ref)\n   561\t                            (throw (ex-info\n   562\t                                     \"Ref resolves to no instruction of this segment\"\n   563\t                                     {:entity e, :ref ref}))))\n   564\t          decode (fn [e]\n   565\t                   (let [ia (get attrs e)\n   566\t                         mnem (:yin.code/op ia)\n   567\t                         opcode (or (get vm/opcode-table\n   719\t(defn load-vector\n   720\t  \"Load one canonical instruction vector (UCF §7.3.2) by the direct path\n   721\t   (§7.1): validate it against §7.5 — a defect throws naming the pc — then\n   722\t   decode the positional operands into the same image `load-image` builds\n   723\t   from the projected batch, and register it under `:code` with the\n   724\t   vector's address `(jing/segment-key v)` in the alias column.\n   725\t\n   726\t   A vector claims no local id, so one is minted below the loaded floor\n   727\t   (`vm/loaded-code-floor`), as `ast-loader` mints for lowered AST batches;\n   728\t   an address already aliased reloads under its id, which `store-image`\n   729\t   accepts as the identical image. Options:\n   730\t     :id claim this local segment id instead of minting one. The §3.1 rule\n   731\t          applies: an id already holding a different image is a load error,\n   732\t          an identical reload is accepted. Ignored when the address is\n   733\t          already aliased.\"\n   734\t  ([vm v] (load-vector vm v {}))\n   735\t  ([vm v opts]\n   736\t   (when-let [defect (code/well-formed-vector? v)]\n   737\t     (throw (ex-info (str \"Cannot load vector: \" (name (:rule defect))\n   738\t                          \" (pc \" (:pc defect) \")\")\n   739\t                     {:defect defect})))\n   740\t   (let [address (jing/segment-key v)\n   741\t         aliases (:code-aliases vm)\n   742\t         seg (or (get aliases address)\n   743\t                 (:id opts)\n   744\t                 (dec (vm/loaded-code-floor (:code vm))))\n   745\t         image {:segment seg,\n   746\t                :length (count v),\n   747\t                :code (mapv decode-tuple v),\n   748\t                :address address}]\n   749\t     (assoc vm\n   750\t            :program seg\n   751\t            :code (store-image (:code vm) image)\n   752\t            :code-aliases (store-alias aliases image)\n   753\t            :control {:segment seg, :pc 0}\n   754\t            :stack []\n   755\t            :k nil\n   756\t            :halted? false\n   757\t            :blocked? false\n   758\t            :value nil))))\n   759\t\n   760\t\n   761\t;; =============================================================================\n   762\t;; SemanticVM Protocol Implementation\n   763\t;; =============================================================================\n   764\t\n   765\t(defn- vm-reset\n   766\t  \"Reset execution state, preserving loaded code.\"\n   767\t  [vm]\n   768\t  (assoc vm\n   769\t         :control (when-let [seg (:program vm)] {:segment seg, :pc 0})\n   770\t         :k nil\n   132\t        (let [body0 (first (:bodies segment))\n   133\t              reg-count (or (:registers body0) 0)]\n   134\t          (assoc vm\n   135\t                 :segment segment\n   136\t                 :hash (rcode/register-hash segment)\n   137\t                 :pc 0\n   138\t                 :frames []\n   139\t                 :registers (vec (repeat reg-count nil))\n   140\t                 :continuation []\n   141\t                 :halted? false\n   142\t                 :blocked? false\n   143\t                 :value nil))))))\n   144\t\n   145\t\n   146\t(defn create-vm\n   147\t  \"Build a fresh `DebruijnRegisterVM` over `segment`.\n   148\t   Options: `:free-env`, `:store`, `:primitives`, `:modules`, `:make-stream`,\n   149\t   `:call-in`/`:call-out`/`:call-capacity`, and `:bridge`.\"\n   150\t  ([segment] (create-vm segment {}))\n724:(defn vm-load-rows\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
