{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '85,115p;1620,1640p'\"","aggregated_output":"    85\t1. The namespace `yin.vm.linker` and its migration from\n    86\t   `yin.vm.debruijn-linker` (section 9).\n    87\t2. Two new format records, `:yin.ast/code` and `:yin.semantic/code`, beside\n    88\t   the two B6 records (section 5).\n    89\t3. A `:parts-fn` slot in the format record so that a multi-row payload\n    90\t   (an AST tree) fetches through the same pipeline as a single vector,\n    91\t   with row-local validation and composition-supplied bounds before any\n    92\t   child is enqueued (section 4.2, step 2).\n    93\t4. Identity-directed matching: `:identity-matches-fn` replaces a bare\n    94\t   hash comparison, so storage-derived identities verify under the\n    95\t   algorithm the identity carries (section 4.1).\n    96\t5. Dependency obligations `{name kind expected}` replacing bare free\n    97\t   names, net of the module's own definitions, discharged by exact\n    98\t   profile or manifest equality at the receiver (section 4.2, step 5).\n    99\t6. The stepped link interface (`link-state`, `request-link`, `step`,\n   100\t   `abandon`) as the portable shape, with a plain-data wire request and\n   101\t   all indexes and capabilities held in linker-local state; the\n   102\t   synchronous `fetch` is reclassified as host policy over an explicit\n   103\t   link runtime (section 6).\n   104\t7. The `:module/require` effect lowered onto the linker: two wait\n   105\t   states, cursor-before-append, pair-scoped id correlation,\n   106\t   installation as a scheduler child task, and export relocation by\n   107\t   lift and lower (section 7).\n   108\t8. The module manifest, pinned to one canonical tree by content-addressed\n   109\t   derivation records verified by re-lowering or explicitly trusted,\n   110\t   and the manifest registry that replaces the in-memory module\n   111\t   dictionary (section 8).\n   112\t9. A fail-closed, proof-carrying name-authority policy for `dao.space`\n   113\t   assertions, an entry criterion for M4 (section 8.2).\n   114\t10. Eleven additional refusals (section 4.3).\n   115\t\n  1620\t    never installed; under `:trusted` the same manifest installs with\n  1621\t    `:trust :composition` in the outcome.\n  1622\t19. A request naming a mismatched contract is refused with no content\n  1623\t    request appended and no validator run.\n  1624\t20. A closure re-exported from a transitive dependency lifts with that\n  1625\t    dependency's image as origin, the parent loads that image before\n  1626\t    lowering, and an origin the scheduler never verified is\n  1627\t    `:foreign-image`; a positional marker offered to a named kernel is\n  1628\t    `:binding-mismatch`.\n  1629\t21. A replayed envelope, an envelope at or below a principal's floor,\n  1630\t    two envelopes with one sequence, a retraction naming no assertion,\n  1631\t    and a retraction by another principal are each discarded with the\n  1632\t    stated kind; a retraction bound to an assertion's id removes that\n  1633\t    assertion only.\n  1634\t22. One four-way manifest links through all four kernels with no\n  1635\t    `:contract-mismatch`; a manifest of another schema version is\n  1636\t    `:descriptor-defect` with rule `:schema`; a derivation without a\n  1637\t    contract entry is `:descriptor-defect` with rule\n  1638\t    `:contract-missing`.\n  1639\t\n  1640\t## 12. Open decisions\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
