gment ($code). They\n  1380\t;; supply the fixed point's inputs; the value, name-satisfaction, and\n  1381\t;; module parts remain the walk UCF §7.6.1 specifies. Free names are\n  1382\t;; `free-names` above; everything else the syntactic queries fill is here.\n  1383\t\n  1384\t(def footprint-table\n  1385\t  \"§7.7.1's effect normalization as a data value, keyed by the execution\n  1386\t   contract stamp (UCF §7.3.3) — the effect a syntax tag or mnemonic raises\n  1387\t   is part of that contract, lifted out of the reference machine's hot loop\n  1388\t   (`semantic.cljc`). Two directions: `:tags` over every §2.3 syntax tag\n  1389\t   and `:mnemonics` over every §2.4 mnemonic, each to the set of effect\n  1390\t   identifiers it contributes. Every tag and every mnemonic has a row, so\n  1391\t   \\\"no external effect\\\" is an explicit `#{}`, never an absence; a tag or\n  1392\t   mnemonic outside the table is `:yin.k/undecodable`, the outcome the\n  1393\t   validators give it — and the extraction queries' tag/mnemonic sets are\n  1394\t   table subsets, so over validated rows the lookup is total. The design\n  1395\t   table's tag↔mnemonic correspondence is 1:1 for the effect rows and\n  1396\t   deliberately lumped for the last (5 tags lower to 9 mnemonics; see\n  1397\t   `yin.vm.linearize`), so it is not re-stated as a map here. Its \\\"other\n  1398\t   requirement\\\" column is realized by the extraction queries themselves:\n  1399\t   an FFI op goes to the receiver-capability requirement\n  1400\t   (`:yin.k/ffi-ops` — the pair's own store keys are never a store-slice\n  1401\t   requirement, UCF §7.6.2), a store key to the store slice, a parked id\n  1402\t   to the parked-record obligation, and a call's effects are its callee's\n  1403\t   profile effects (§7.7.2). A `:variable`'s name obligation is\n  1404\t   conditional on freeness (§4.5) — a query (`free-names`), not a\n  1405\t   per-tag footprint fact.\"\n  1406\t  {\"v2\"\n  1407\t   {:tags {:stream/make #{:stream/make},\n  1408\t           :stream/put #{:stream/put},\n  1409\t           :stream/cursor #{:stream/cursor},\n  1410\t           :stream/next #{:stream/next},\n  1500\t     :parked-ids (extract (:parked-ids queries) db),\n  1501\t     :effects (into #{} (mapcat table) (extract (:effect-raisers queries) db))}))\n  1502\t\n  1503\t\n  1504\t(defn ast-requirements\n  1505\t  \"§7.7's syntactic requirement set from a tree relation `$ast` — a\n  1506\t   `query/relation` over the flat rows of the reachable trees (e.g.\n  1507\t   `(vals (:rows (ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))`, unioned across trees):\n  1508\t   store keys, FFI ops, parked ids, and effect identifiers, effects\n  1509\t   already normalized by the footprint table. These are the fields of\n  1510\t   `:yin.k/requires` the syntactic queries fill; free names are\n  1511\t   `free-names`, and the value/name/module parts of UCF §7.6.1's fixed\n  1512\t   point remain the walk that consumes this.\"\n  1513\t  [db]\n  1514\t  (requirements db ast-extraction-queries :tags))\n  1515\t\n  1516\t\n  1517\t(defn segment-requirements\n  1518\t  \"The same over a `$code` relation of segment-qualified rows\n  1519\t   (`yin.vm.code/project-segment-qualified`). For every tree,\n  1520\t   `(ast-requirements tree-relation)` and this over its lowered segment's\n  1521\t   rows are equal in every field — the §7.7.1 conformance obligation.\"\n  1522\t  [db]\n  1523\t  (requirements db segment-extraction-queries :mnemonics))\n  1524\t\n  1525\t\n  1526\t(def ^:private many-attrs #{:yin/operands :yin/args :yin/params})\n  1527\t\n  1528\t\n  1529\t(defn index-datoms\n  1530\t  \"Index AST datoms by entity.\n  1531\t   Returns {:by-entity map, :get-attr fn, :root-id int}, plus\n  1532\t   `:error {:rule :dangling-root :entity e}` when the root fact names an\n  1533\t   entity with no `:yin/type`.\n  1534\t\n  1535\t   The root is the entity of the last `:yin/root` fact in batch order. A\n  1536\t   batch with no root fact falls back to the structural heuristic below. A\n  1537\t   dangling root is recorded, not thrown: the index still names it, and\n  1538\t   decoding it is what fails loudly.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
